Rapid Testing Module User Guide

This module is designed to help users analyze, test the impact of different options, and optimize water distribution networks with ease.
________________________________________
1. Getting Started
First-Time Setup
1.	Import Your Network – Click “Import Net” (top-left) and select your EPANET .INP file
If you don’t have a file, the app will use a built-in example network
2.	The Main Dashboard – Your network data loads automatically, and you’ll see:
o	A table showing network elements (pipes, junctions, tanks, etc.)
o	Analysis report panel (right side)
o	Control panel (left side)
________________________________________
2. Understanding the Interface
Left Panel – Network Controls
•	Element type dropdown: Select what you want to analyze (Pipes, Junctions, Tanks, etc.)
•	Element Name dropdown: Choose the specific element from your network
•	Attribute dropdown: Pick which characteristic to modify (diameter, pressure, demand, etc.)
•	Options table: Where you create different scenarios to test
Right Panel – Results & Reports
•	Analysis Report: Shows detailed simulation results
•	Export buttons: Save reports as PDF or HTML
•	Expand/Collapse: Toggle report visibility
Bottom Section – Action Buttons
•	Run Simulation: Test your modified network
•	Graphical Tools: Create charts and animations
•	Export Options: Save your network or data
________________________________________
3. Core Workflow – Testing Different Scenarios
Step 1: Select What to Test
1.	From “Element type”, choose (e.g., “Pipe”)
2.	From “Element Name”, pick a specific pipe
3.	From “Attribute”, select what to change (e.g., “Diameter”)
Step 2: Create Multiple Options
1.	Number of Options: Set how many variations to test (default: 10)
2.	Start Value: Enter the starting value (e.g., current diameter: 0.3)
3.	Increment by: How much to increase each option (e.g., 0.01)
4.	Click “AutoFill” – The table automatically fills with your options
Step 3: Run the Analysis
1.	Click “Run Simulation and Report” (red button)
2.	Wait for processing – a progress bar shows analysis status
3.	View results in the Analysis Report panel
Step 4: Compare Results
•	Each “Option” in your table becomes a separate scenario
•	The report compares all options side-by-side
•	Critical metrics are highlighted (pressure issues, water quality, etc.)
