6. Practical Examples
Example 1: Testing Pipe Diameter Changes
1.	Select: Element type = Pipe, Element name = Pipe-10, Attribute = Diameter
2.	Set: Start Value = 0.3, Increment = 0.02, Options = 8
3.	Click AutoFill → Run Simulation
4.	Result: See how increasing diameter affects pressure and flow
Example 2: Adjusting Tank Levels
1.	Select: Element type = Tank, Attribute = Initial Level
2.	Create options with different starting levels
3.	Run simulation to see impact on system pressure
Example 3: Demand Pattern Testing
1.	Select: Element type = Junction, Attribute = Demand Pattern
2.	Test different consumption scenarios
3.	Identify peak demand impacts
