7. Understanding Results
Key Metrics Explained
•	Pressure: Should stay above minimum requirements (red flags if too low)
•	Water Age: How long water stays in system (ideal: <24 hours)
•	Flow Rate: Volume moving through pipes
•	Headloss: Pressure loss in pipes
•	Demand: Water consumption at different points
Reading the Report
•	Green text: Normal operation
•	Warning sections: Potential issues identified
•	Comparative tables: Option 1 vs Option 2 vs Option 3...
•	Time steps: Analysis at different hours (0-23)
________________________________________
8. Tips & Best Practices
For Accurate Results
1.	Always start with a valid EPANET .INP file
2.	Create small increments between options initially
3.	Run baseline (original network) first for comparison
4.	Focus on one change at a time for clear cause-effect analysis
Performance Tips
•	Close other applications during large simulations
•	Use fewer options (5-10) for quicker results
•	The “Significant Figures” button controls decimal precision
Troubleshooting
•	No results? Ensure network imported successfully
•	Missing elements? Check your .INP file contains the elements
•	Calculation errors? Try smaller value increments
•	Contact Support: Use “Contact Us” for technical issues
